 R←Test_API_026(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;buff;filename1;filename2;hash1;hash2;folder
⍝ Exercises what only the ready-made fixture Proj_4 offers: a file in the root of the project,
⍝ and a file that was changed by more than two commits.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 folder←''

 ⍝ A file in the ROOT of the project carries no path separator, yet it is not an APL name:
 →T.PassesIf'README.md'≡⊃∆Folder4 G.IdentifyObject'README.md'

 ⍝ A bare filename that is neither an APL object nor in the root: the source folder is searched
 →T.PassesIf'APLSource/Counter.aplf'≡⊃∆Folder4 G.IdentifyObject'Counter.aplf'

 ⍝ The same file, this time addressed relative to the root, with and without "./":
 →T.PassesIf'APLSource/Counter.aplf'≡⊃∆Folder4 G.IdentifyObject'APLSource/Counter.aplf'
 →T.PassesIf'APLSource/Counter.aplf'≡⊃∆Folder4 G.IdentifyObject'./APLSource/Counter.aplf'

 ⍝ Counter.aplf was changed by three commits, README.md by two:
 →T.PassesIf 3=≢∆Folder4 G.ChangeLog'Counter.aplf'
 →T.PassesIf 2=≢∆Folder4 G.ChangeLog'README.md'

 ⍝ Comparing the two most recent versions of Counter.aplf must yield 3 and 2:
 (filename1 filename2 hash1 hash2)←∆Folder4 G.CompareVersions'Counter.aplf'
 folder←⊃⎕NPARTS filename1
 →T.GoToTidyUp hash1≡hash2
 →T.GoToTidyUp' r←3'≢2⊃⊃⎕NGET filename1 1
 →T.GoToTidyUp' r←2'≢2⊃⊃⎕NGET filename2 1

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 :If 0<≢folder
     {}FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce folder
 :EndIf
⍝Done
